cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Trust, but verify: making GENCO safe for N-k contingency screening"
abstract: >-
  An audit of GENCO, the GridFM power-flow foundation model, for N-k contingency screening on the Texas 2,000-bus grid;
  a verification workflow in which Newton-Raphson decides and every case ends verified safe, verified violation or
  unresolved; and two extensions of GENCO: fine-tuning on solver-labelled contingencies and a warning head that predicts
  unresolved cases from GENCO's embeddings. The workflow test is repeated on IEEE 118 with the GENCO released for it.
